course: dictionary
lesson: 5155
title: Iroquois: a name for a people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Iroquois is a name, and it names a group of Native American nations, also called the Haudenosaunee. Iroquois can also name their languages and their league of nations. «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy, also called the Iroquois, joined five, later six, nations in a lasting alliance.» The two names in that sentence point to the same people.
explain: Context helps you see that the Iroquois are many nations, not one. The sentence says they joined five, later six, nations. So the Iroquois are a group of nations that came together in an alliance, which means they agreed to work together.
explain: Iroquois can be a noun, as in «the Iroquois» or «an Iroquois», or an adjective, as in «Iroquois languages». Many people today prefer their own name, Haudenosaunee, so when you write or speak about them, use that name where you can.
fact: The Iroquois are a group of Native American nations, also called the Haudenosaunee.
fact: The Iroquois lived in what is now New York State and parts of Canada.
fact: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy, also called the Iroquois, joined five, later six, nations in a lasting alliance.»
fact: The five nations were Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca, and the Tuscarora joined later.
fact: Many people today prefer the name Haudenosaunee, which is their own name for themselves.
exercise: «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy, also called the Iroquois, joined five, later six, nations in a lasting alliance.» In this sentence, what does Iroquois name? | A river in Canada | *The same group of nations as the Haudenosaunee | A single small village | A kind of food
exercise: Which nation joined the Confederacy later than the others? | Seneca | *Tuscarora | Mohawk | Oneida
exercise: Many people today prefer which name for their nations? | Mohawk | *Haudenosaunee | Longhouse | Iroquois
test: In «Iroquois languages», what kind of word is Iroquois? | *Adjective | Noun | Adverb | Verb
test: Which foods did the Iroquois grow? | Potatoes and wheat | *Corn, beans and squash | Oranges and grapes | Rice and tea
exam: Which is the best reason to use the name Haudenosaunee? | *Because many people today prefer their own name | Because Iroquois is a rude word | Because it is the shortest name | Because it is found in every history book
